From cb88ef9afb52e41adaab96cef3727a1bdd32e35c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: muham <mhammar029@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:17:42 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] windows: call log (BLINDLY4_LOG), --at UNIX_SECONDS,
 press --under with title/role/identifier

- BLINDLY4_LOG=FILE makes every invocation append one JSON line (start time, duration,
  BLINDLY4_LOG_TAG, arguments, exit code, stdout); concurrent writers serialize on the file.
- --at UNIX_SECONDS (any command) waits until that moment, then runs it; the accessibility
  deadline starts after the wait. Lets a slow caller time an action to about 0.1 s.
- press --under PATH [--title] [--role] [--identifier] [--depth] presses the first match below
  PATH as the tree is when the press runs, so a press scheduled with --at survives a page
  renumbering its children (YouTube's control bar does).

